A||||14||DaRkLoRD||Chevy Cavalier digital gauges in a Fiero?||||1||
Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||11-29-1999||06:57 PM||||I've heard from several people on a kitcar newsgroup as well as from the Fiero mailing list, that it is possible to put the instrument cluster from an 87 Chevy cavalier into a Fiero. I've seen pictures of one installed in a Fiero, but not when the car was running.<P>From what I hear, the dash plugs into the same sending units that the Fiero uses.. essentially a direct replacement. Has anyone here tried this, or know anyone who has?<BR>Basically I'd like to find out if this works as claimed, what the top speed of the speedometer is on the Cavalier dash, etc.<P>thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||11-29-1999||07:18 PM||||I had my mom's old 87 Z-24 well over 100 before and the speedo showed it. It is a pretty neat looking dash, but her's had to be replaced twice due to some unknown defect, the first time when the car only had about 20,000 miles on it. Some Buick cars also has a neat looking digital dash- Riveria and Reatta I believe. I have always thought the touch screen system in the Reatta would be really cool in the Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000002||chris6878||11-29-1999||08:36 PM||||my dads 87 buick somerset has the digital dash also...  everything  oddometer, speedo, temp, and so on.. all digital..   <P>that would be neat to have a digital dash like that in a fiero...  hmmmm||||reg||10
Z||000003||theogre||11-29-1999||09:34 PM||||Friend of mine had the digidash in an 85 cavalier. It almost never worked right. I didn't like it much when it did work. The tach is really annoying.||||reg||1
Z||000004||2FAST4U||11-29-1999||09:58 PM||||If you guy's really want a digital dash, then contact Dakota Digital. They can build a custom panel, convert your panel, anything you can think oy they can build and with any color numerals. They arn't very expensive either. <BR>If anyone is interested let me know and I'll get there address and phone number for you.<p>[This message has been edited by 2FAST4U (edited 11-29-1999).]||||reg||1
