Z||000007||DaRkLoRD||11-30-1999||05:43 PM||||I wrote a reply to this message this afternoon, but got a message saying the forum was down for maintenance.. now I guess I'll have to try and remember it again!<P>My goal is a totally custom interior, so the FDD-X1 isn't exactly what I'm looking for. (gauge pod won't be the same as the stock fiero one) It's an incredibly cool product though. Very well designed, looks awesome. <P>Oh, btw, I wouldn't call Dakota Digital inexpensive.. $500 USD was the lowest price I saw for "custom" gauges. ouch.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cliff Pennock||11-30-1999||06:54 PM||||DJRice, I don't mind at all that other digital gauges are being mentioned.<P>In fact, if I would find one that had more options and/or looked better than mine, I would swap it in a heartbeat! Needless to say I haven't seen one yet...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Seriously, I don't mind the competition at all and it's really a matter of personal taste which digital gauges one would choose. I know that's not really a business point of view... I know my competitors are having a completely opposite look on this. I've seen them dish the FDD-X1 on public messageboards (while they had never seen it). I even received an email from the guy who has made the &lt;brandname deleted&gt; dash, accusing me from stealing his design. That would be very clever from my part - since I have never seen his dash up close. Some guys just can't stand the competition. Me? I don't care!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
